 ## Overview
 
-DCX Points-to-Voxels converts a set of 3D points into a sparse voxel grid representation by mapping each point to a discrete voxel index within a defined bounding box, storing occupancy in a 3D integer array, and computing the centroid of points within each occupied voxel [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It differs from simple averaging by prioritizing points with higher depth confidence in its aggregation step, which helps mitigate noise and outliers in regions with uncertain geometry [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the final aggregation step in the DCX pipeline, refining the raw point cloud into a structured sparse representation suitable for downstream rendering or reconstruction tasks [S1, unofficial], contrasting with direct occupancy mapping in [VoxelGrid::CreateFromPointCloudWithinBounds](8505-voxelgrid-createfrompointcloudwithinbounds.md) or multi-plane approaches in [Multi-Plane Point Cloud Voxelization and Weight Aggregation](12101-multi-plane-point-cloud-voxelization-and-weight-aggregation.md).
+DCX Points-to-Voxels converts a set of 3D points into a sparse voxel grid representation by mapping each point to a discrete voxel index within a defined bounding box, storing occupancy in a 3D integer array, and computing the centroid of points within each occupied voxel [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It differs from simple averaging by prioritizing points with higher depth confidence in its aggregation step, which helps mitigate noise and outliers in regions with uncertain geometry [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the final aggregation step in the DCX pipeline, refining the raw point cloud into a structured sparse representation suitable for downstream rendering or reconstruction tasks [S1, unofficial]. It contrasts with direct occupancy mapping in [VoxelGrid::CreateFromPointCloudWithinBounds](8505-voxelgrid-createfrompointcloudwithinbounds.md) or multi-plane approaches in [Multi-Plane Point Cloud Voxelization and Weight Aggregation](12101-multi-plane-point-cloud-voxelization-and-weight-aggregation.md).
 
